from pathlib import Path
import json
ROOT=Path(__file__).parent
bank=json.loads((ROOT/'interview-category-bank.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
templates=[
 dict(id='GENERAL',nature='General factual discovery',title='General applicant interview',families=['DEC','CHD','MON','INT','TIM','EVD']),
 dict(id='NULLITY',nature='Annulment-related factual inquiry',title='Decision and circumstances at marriage',families=['DEC','CHD','MON','INT','PRS','DBT','WED','CON','BKG','TIM','EVD']),
 dict(id='BREAKDOWN',nature='Divorce / dissolution',title='Marriage breakdown and reconciliation',families=['CHD','MON','INT','TIM','SEP','REC','EVD']),
 dict(id='INFIDELITY',nature='Divorce / dissolution',title='Infidelity inquiry',families=['INF','TIM','EVD']),
 dict(id='ABANDONMENT',nature='Divorce / dissolution',title='Desertion / abandonment inquiry',families=['ABD','TIM','SEP','REC','EVD']),
 dict(id='ABUSE',nature='Divorce / dissolution',title='Abuse inquiry',families=['ABU','TIM','EVD']),
 dict(id='FAITH',nature='Divorce / dissolution',title='Leaving or changing the faith',families=['FTH','TIM','EVD']),
 dict(id='ADDICTION',nature='Divorce / dissolution',title='Addiction inquiry',families=['ADD','TIM','REC','EVD']),
 dict(id='CONCEALMENT',nature='Relevant petition / selected ground',title='Misrepresentation or concealment',families=['CON','DEC','TIM','EVD'])]
structure={'title':'Case Investigation and Factual Discovery','status':'Planning presets for review, not canonical rules or a production feature. Template selection does not change case type or prior answers.','templates':templates,'bank':bank}
(ROOT/'investigation-structure.json').write_text(json.dumps(structure,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
master='''You are helping refine CTM, an Orthodox church tribunal application, not providing a diagnosis, treatment plan, legal advice or a canonical judgment.

Use the attached CTM question bank and accepted decisions as the source of existing coverage. We need precise, neutral factual-discovery prompts, not a counseling session or a full personal biography. Research counseling/marital relationship literature only where it adds a defensible factual distinction missing from this bank. Prefer primary peer-reviewed research or official professional/institutional sources; give direct links and distinguish research support from institutional/doctrinal applicability. Do not invent citations or present Catholic procedures as Orthodox rules.

Workflow: petition nature -> template -> reusable common question family -> detailed questions -> attributed answers/evidence -> assembled report. The same family is reused, not copied. Mandatory interview/recording identity opening and shared chronology/source/evidence prompts are already present. Children, Money and Intimacy are explicit families. Do not repeat these core questions inside every category. Medical/psychiatric testing and disclosure needs signed, scoped release; no blanket records request or diagnostic inference. Do not upload real case data or medical reports to an AI.

Applicant submission, manual interview answer, original recording, reviewed transcript, submitted priest report and council finding are separate records. An affair statement is an allegation; a submitted date can be confirmed, not silently overwritten. Never disclose one applicant's private material to the other. No AI extraction into questionnaire answers is approved. No generic communication, multi-ceremony, full prior-marriage interview or separate appeal question module is to be reintroduced; those proposals were rejected. General witness/priest interviews are out of scope; a separately requested free-form priest testimony report is different.

First test whether the existing question or another family already covers the fact. Return NO ADDITION if it does. At most three narrowly justified follow-ups for an identified gap. For each proposed follow-up give: exact wording; family and stable question reference; the concrete fact sought; trigger/skip condition; why it is not redundant; existing question to refine rather than duplicate; source/evidence limits; possible evidence links; and whether wording needs institutional review. No new required fields, grounds, third-party access, proof threshold, diagnosis or legal rule. Explain how a counseling-source idea differs from a neutral tribunal inquiry.

Return English review wording first. Optional Arabic translation must be labeled a draft. Never imply an unknown or unanswered fact is affirmative. Preserve exact versus approximate dates, occurrence versus discovery, direct versus reported knowledge, and statement versus finding. If a research question cannot be supported, say so. Recommendations remain proposals for human review.'''
axes={
'DEC':'Separate the actual decision, reasons, communicated agreements and later knowledge; do not decide validity.',
'CHD':'Distinguish stated pre-marriage expectations, communication, later change and concrete relevant parenting events. No child testimony or universal reproductive history.',
'MON':'Distinguish what was discussed/disclosed, known debt/income facts, concrete decisions and alleged concealment. No general financial audit.',
'INT':'Stay within the voluntarily described specific intimate difficulty and its timing/relevance. No intrusive inventory or diagnosis.',
'PRS':'Distinguish specific conduct/threat, source/timing and described effect on decision. Do not label family participation coercion automatically.',
'DBT':'Distinguish a communicated serious reservation, response and subsequent choice from hindsight alone.',
'WED':'Investigate a specific relevant event near the ceremony, without creating a new clinical or canonical test.',
'CON':'Distinguish representation, fact allegedly concealed, importance at the time, discovery and corroboration; preserve different assertions.',
'INF':'Distinguish allegation, firsthand observation, hearsay and document provenance; avoid presuming guilt or adding irrelevant sexual detail.',
'ABD':'Distinguish known absence/contact/support from inferred intent; preserve unknowns and absent-spouse allowances.',
'ABU':'Use concrete relevant acts/patterns and source certainty. Do not compel a detailed traumatic biography, diagnose or question children.',
'FTH':'Distinguish earlier affiliation, later practice/affiliation change, evidence and described marital effect; no doctrinal conclusion from attendance.',
'ADD':'Distinguish reported behavior, timing, effect and known help, not a diagnosis from a checkbox.',
'BKG':'Allow only a demonstrable connection to the issue; no full childhood/sexual/family history.',
'TIM':'Refine time distinctions only if not covered already; occurrence/discovery and exact/approximate/unknown are core.',
'SEP':'Separate temporary intervals, final separation and reunion; do not copy an entire rejected application separation form.',
'REC':'Record actual assistance, participation and observed outcome without confessional disclosure or a psychiatric inference.',
'EVD':'Preserve provenance, asserted fact, exact source version, knowledge limits and contradictory material; do not require external witness accounts.',
'MED':'Topic approved: relevant medical/psychiatric evaluations with signed release. Exact question wording still pending. Be explicit about medical, psychological or psychiatric help without requesting blanket records or diagnosing.'}
prompts=['# Research prompts for interview question refinement','',
'Use these with another AI if deeper research is needed. Send the master prompt and the relevant category/question prompt, plus the anonymized question bank. No real applicant identities, case evidence, recordings or medical records are needed. These prompts are not an instruction to publish new questions automatically.','',
'## Master prompt','', '```text',master,'```','',
'## Category prompts','']
question_prompts=[]
for c in bank['categories']:
 text=f"Family: {c['title']} ({c['id']}). Status: {'wording pending' if c['pending'] else 'expanded draft for review'}.\nFocus: {axes[c['id']]}\nExisting questions:\n"+'\n'.join(f"{q['id']}: {q['text']}"for q in c['questions'])+'\nApply the master prompt. Compare all shared core/families before suggesting changes. Return no addition if the existing coverage is sufficient.'
 prompts+=['### '+c['title'],'','```text',text,'```','']
for c in bank['categories']:
 prompts+=['## Per-question prompts: '+c['title'],'']
 for q in c['questions']:
  text=f"Apply the CTM master prompt to {q['id']} in {c['title']}.\nCurrent wording: {q['text']}\nSpecific focus: {axes[c['id']]}\nCompare the sibling questions and common chronology/source/evidence questions in the supplied bank. Identify only a missing factual distinction. Propose a clearer replacement before adding a follow-up. Give NO CHANGE if adequate; otherwise provide exact wording, source link, trigger/skip rule, non-duplication rationale and institutional-review limits. Do not expand scope merely to generate more questions."
  prompts+=['### '+q['id'],'','```text',text,'```','']
  question_prompts.append({'id':q['id'],'family':c['id'],'prompt':text})
for b in bank['fixedBlocks']:
 prompts+=['## Common block prompts: '+b['title'],'']
 for i,text in enumerate(b['questions'],1):
  qid=f'{b["id"]}-{i:02}'
  prompt=f'Apply the CTM master prompt to {qid}: {text}\nKeep the mandatory identity/recording opening or common request/closing purpose intact. Do not duplicate any substantive family. Suggest only a concrete clarity correction supported by the source; otherwise return NO CHANGE. No new oath, signature, diagnosis, canonical rule or applicant disclosure.'
  prompts+=['### '+qid,'','```text',prompt,'```',''];question_prompts.append({'id':qid,'family':b['id'],'prompt':prompt})
(ROOT.parent/'CTM-category-research-prompts.md').write_text('\n'.join(prompts)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
(ROOT/'category-research-prompts.json').write_text(json.dumps({'master':master,'categories':axes,'questionPrompts':question_prompts},ensure_ascii=False,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
css=(ROOT.parent/'questionnaire/questionnaire.css').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>CTM Case Investigation and Factual Discovery</title><style>'''+css+'''
main{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(270px,350px) minmax(0,1fr);gap:32px}aside{position:static}.category-select{display:flex;gap:9px;padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.category-select input{margin-top:5px;accent-color:var(--accent)}small{display:block;color:var(--muted)}.pending{opacity:.65}.section{padding:20px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.question{margin:9px 0}.context{padding:13px;background:var(--soft);font-size:14px}.controls{display:grid;gap:10px}.controls label{font-size:14px;font-weight:600}select{font:inherit;width:100%;padding:8px;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);border:1px solid #88978f}.context-heading{font-weight:700}.links{display:flex;gap:15px;flex-wrap:wrap}.outline{font-size:14px}.notice{padding:15px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}@media(max-width:800px){main{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style></head><body><header><p class="eyebrow">CTM / architecture planning preview</p><h1>Case Investigation<br>and Factual Discovery.</h1><p class="intro">Petition nature → template → reusable common question family → detailed questions → report.</p><p>Switch between template and family views without changing selected questions. The same family is reused across templates. This is a planning preview, not a place for real case data; no recording, signing, medical upload or CTM feature is implemented.</p><p class="links"><a href="../CTM-investigation-model.md">Architecture and medical-release rules</a><a href="../CTM-category-research-prompts.md">Research prompts for every category/question</a><a href="../CTM-priest-testimony-template-draft.md">Free-form priest report</a></p></header><main><aside><h2>Organize the interview</h2><div class="controls"><label for="nature">Petition nature</label><select id="nature"></select><label for="template">Template</label><select id="template"></select><label for="view">View templates</label><select id="view"><option value="template">By petition / template</option><option value="family">By common question family</option></select><button id="suggested" type="button">Add template’s suggested families</button></div><p class="small">These are review presets, not canonical rules. All other approved families remain available. Changing a view/preset never silently removes selected material. Medical interview wording is pending independently of the approved tests/release requirement.</p><div id="categories"></div><p id="count" role="status"></p><button id="clear" type="button">Clear selections</button></aside><section><h2>Questionnaire and report outline</h2><p class="outline">Exact application answers and submitted evidence appear as attributed context—not as new, independently editable copies. Report sections use recorded answers; observations and reviewed transcript references remain separate.</p><div id="report"></div><div class="notice"><h2>Medical / psychiatric evaluations</h2><p>Conditional applicant and council records link the subject, relevant test/evaluation, retained report and signed release disclosure. No universal testing. Release text/version, signature/date and permitted purpose/recipients stay identifiable. No medical-document disclosure, search or external AI sharing is inferred from ordinary upload acceptance.</p></div><div class="notice"><h2>Assembled report</h2><p>Interview/subject metadata · exact template/family/question versions · selected detailed questions and actual answers · source confirmation/evidence links · separately authored observations · original audio/reviewed transcript references. No AI-filled answers or case export.</p></div></section></main><footer>Planning artifact · no real case data collected · new detailed wording remains draft</footer><script>const MODEL=__MODEL__;
const BANK=MODEL.bank,selected=new Set();const el=id=>document.getElementById(id);const make=(tag,text)=>{const n=document.createElement(tag);n.textContent=text;return n;};
function current(){return MODEL.templates.find(t=>t.id===el('template').value)||MODEL.templates[0];}
function fillTemplates(){el('template').replaceChildren();for(const t of MODEL.templates.filter(t=>t.nature===el('nature').value)){const o=make('option',t.title);o.value=t.id;el('template').append(o);}el('template').value=MODEL.templates.find(t=>t.nature===el('nature').value).id;render();}
function block(title,questions){const s=make('section','');s.className='section';s.append(make('h2',title));for(const q of questions){const p=make('p',q.id+' · '+q.text);p.className='question';s.append(p);}return s;}
function context(s,title,text){const box=make('div','');box.className='context';box.append(make('p',title),make('p',text));s.append(box);}
function render(){
 const t=current(),families=[...BANK.categories];if(el('view').value==='template')families.sort((a,b)=>Number(t.families.includes(b.id))-Number(t.families.includes(a.id)));else families.sort((a,b)=>a.title.localeCompare(b.title));
 el('categories').replaceChildren();for(const c of families){const l=make('label','');l.className='category-select'+(c.pending?' pending':'');const box=document.createElement('input');box.type='checkbox';box.value=c.id;box.checked=selected.has(c.id);box.disabled=c.pending;box.addEventListener('change',()=>{if(box.checked)selected.add(c.id);else selected.delete(c.id);render();});const txt=make('span','');txt.append(make('strong',c.title),make('small',c.pending?'Exact question wording pending':c.questions.length+' questions'+(t.families.includes(c.id)?' · suggested for this template':'')));l.append(box,txt);el('categories').append(l);}
 const report=el('report');report.replaceChildren();for(const b of BANK.fixedBlocks.slice(0,2)){const s=block(b.title,b.questions.map((text,i)=>({id:b.id+'-'+String(i+1).padStart(2,'0'),text})));if(b.id==='BASIS')context(s,'Example source context — application confirmation','Applicant’s submitted church-marriage date [exact answer revision] and MC certificate [file version]. Ask to confirm or explain; preserve the interview response separately from the original application. No real data shown.');report.append(s);}
 for(const c of BANK.categories)if(selected.has(c.id)&&!c.pending){const s=block(c.title,c.questions);if(c.id==='INF')context(s,'Example source context — submitted affair statement','[Supplying party] statement [exact submission/version/date] alleging an affair → relevant questions and evidence references. Allegation is not a finding. Do not expose the other party’s private material to the interviewee.');if(c.id==='EVD')context(s,'Source-linked inquiry','A question can reference submitted application answers, statements and exact evidence versions, with provider, date and source certainty. No duplicate upload or new applicant attachment-description requirement.');report.append(s);}
 const b=BANK.fixedBlocks[2];report.append(block(b.title,b.questions.map((text,i)=>({id:b.id+'-'+String(i+1).padStart(2,'0'),text}))));el('count').textContent=selected.size+' selected families · view changes preserve selection';
}
for(const nature of new Set(MODEL.templates.map(t=>t.nature))){const o=make('option',nature);o.value=nature;el('nature').append(o);}el('nature').value=MODEL.templates[0].nature;el('view').value='template';
el('nature').addEventListener('change',fillTemplates);el('template').addEventListener('change',render);el('view').addEventListener('change',render);el('suggested').addEventListener('click',()=>{for(const id of current().families){const c=BANK.categories.find(c=>c.id===id);if(c&&!c.pending)selected.add(id);}render();});el('clear').addEventListener('click',()=>{selected.clear();render();});fillTemplates();
</script></body></html>'''
(ROOT/'interview-category-planner.html').write_text(page.replace('__MODEL__',json.dumps(structure,ensure_ascii=False).replace('</','<\\/')),encoding='utf-8')
print('Built petition/template and family views, context examples, and',len(question_prompts),'individual research prompts plus',len(bank['categories']),'category prompts.')
